From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msiexec: /f with a product code repairs the product

msiexec /f accepts a package or the product code of an installed product
(MsiReinstallProduct's argument is the product code); the code form only logged
"Product code treatment not implemented yet" and exited without doing
anything, so a script that repaired by code believed it had. The code is now
given to MsiReinstallProductW with the repair mode the options chose.
---
--- a/programs/msiexec/msiexec.c
+++ b/programs/msiexec/msiexec.c
@@ -1229,8 +1229,15 @@ int WINAPI WinMain(HINSTANCE hInstance, HINSTANCE hPrevInstance, LPSTR lpCmdLine
 	}
 	else if(FunctionRepair)
 	{
+		/* MsiReinstallProduct takes the product code of an installed product */
 		if(IsProductCode(package_unquoted))
+		{
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MSIEXEC_NOCODE
 			WINE_FIXME("Product code treatment not implemented yet\n");
+#else
+			ReturnCode = MsiReinstallProductW(package_unquoted, RepairMode);
+#endif
+		}
 		else
 		{
 			if ((ReturnCode = MsiReinstallProductW(package_unquoted, RepairMode)) == ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND
